      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel adrift when you sense a disconnection from your core self. When the feeling of \"self\" becomes blurry, it can make existence feel meaningless, leading to profound fatigue. Even if the usual feeling of \"you\" feels absent right now, your capacity to feel deeply and question this state is evidence of a living core. Please remember that intense feelings of hopelessness can shift, and even small moments of engagement can slowly start to feel real again.",
      "source": "target",
